.5em!important}\n.rn_text-default .ql-list.ql-indent-6:not(.ql-direction-rtl){padding-left:0!important;margin-left:9em!important}\n.rn_text-default .ql-list.ql-indent-7:not(.ql-direction-rtl){padding-left:0!important;margin-left:10.5em!important}\n.rn_text-default .ql-list.ql-indent-8:not(.ql-direction-rtl){padding-left:0!important;margin-left:12em!important}/* CTA Button styling for email exports */\na.ql-cta-button,.ql-cta-button, a.ql-cta-button:visited{border-radius:0px!important;display:inline-block!important;background-color:#1345ac!important;background-image:none!important;background-position:initial!important;background-repeat:no-repeat!important;padding:12px 24px!important;margin:16px 0!important;text-align:left!important;font-size:14px!important;line-height:14px!important}\na.ql-cta-button{font-family:Arial,\"Helvetica Neue\",Helvetica,sans-serif!important;word-break:break-word!important;font-weight:700!important;color:rgb(255,255,255)!important;text-decoration:none!important;outline:none!important;vertical-align:middle!important}\na.ql-cta-button:hover,.ql-cta-button:hover{opacity:0.95!important}\na.ql-cta-button:hover{color:rgb(255,255,255)!important;text-decoration:none!important}Hey,RouteNote launches new tools available for Dolby Track Mastering - the professional-grade, release-ready mastering service.Since launching on RouteNote earlier this year, Dolby Track Mastering has helped hundreds of independent artists achieve studio quality mastering right on site. Dolby Track Mastering lets any RouteNote users upload a file, customize the audio to their taste, and download a finished file within seconds.This new update brings improvements to the feature users have come to love.Customize OutputYou can now customize your file output. Choose between presets like Streaming, CD Quality, and MP3. Or head to Custom for full access to Output Format (WAV, MP3, FLAC, OPUS, AAC, AIFF, VORBIS), Sample Rate, and Bit Depth options.Your DownloadsSee and download all of your past masters. The new Your Downloads page shows a list of all of your previously mastered tracks. You can search through the list, view the toggles used, and re-download the original or mastered track. Simply click View Downloads from the Dolby Mastering page to see your tracks.These two new features hope to improve your Dolby Track Mastering experience and further push RouteNote as your one-stop shop for all things music.To get started with Dolby Track Mastering, login to your RouteNote account, head to Distribution - Dolby Mastering, or find the shortcut in the Add Audio section of the RouteNote upload process. Find a full step-by-step guide in our preview post.Hear a preview of your track with Dolby Track Mastering for free. Full track downloads are $7.99.Try out Dolby Track MasteringRouteNote TeamPlease note, this email is sent from an unmonitored mailbox. Please\nreach out to\nsupport@routenote.com\nfor any RouteNote enquiries.RouteNote upgrades Dolby Track Mastering RouteNote launches new tools available for Dolby Track Mastering â€“ the professional-grade, release-ready mastering service.Read MoreRouteNote launches Dolby Track Mastering: Professional-grade mastering Master your track with Dolby, to instantly achieve a release-ready, finished product, that sounds consistent across devices.Read MoreAn Artistâ€™s Guide to YouTube - Part 1: The Ultimate Guide to YouTube Official Artists Channels In this four-part series, we\'ll be diving into using one of the most powerful social media platforms as an artist - YouTube.Part one covers YouTube Official Artist Channels (OAC). What they are, how to get one, customizing your channel, and how RouteNote can help you along the way.Watch NowAn Artistâ€™s Guide to YouTube - Part 2: Mastering YouTube Content Part two covers actually creating content, whether thatâ€™s official music videos or more casual content like Shorts. We also take a look at all the stuff that comes along with content, such as thumbnails, descript